# Implementation Details

## UI Structure

The application has a simple UI flow:
1. Upload/drop a video file
2. Configure compression settings (target size and quality priority)
3. Compress the video
4. Preview and download the compressed result

## Key Components

### Video Upload Handling
[compression.js](mdc:compression.js) handles file selection through both direct input and drag-and-drop functionality.

### Compression Logic
The compression algorithm in [compression.js](mdc:compression.js) works by:
1. Calculating target bitrate based on file size and duration
2. Adjusting resolution and quality settings based on user preferences
3. Processing the video frame by frame using canvas
4. Encoding with MediaRecorder API using the most efficient available codec

### Style System
[styles.css](mdc:styles.css) uses CSS variables for consistent theming with a Discord-inspired design system.

## Browser Compatibility

The application requires modern browser features:
- MediaRecorder API
- Canvas API
- File API
- WebM and VP9 support
